<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Big and Small - Races content joined up with three other mods.
		  - The frost jotun gains Alpha Genes' cryo blood and cryo vomit, matching what it is made of.
		  - The Little People faction can roll Det's Stoneborn alongside its own dwarves, with the dwarf chance cut from
		    0.65 to 0.3 to make room for an equal Stoneborn chance.
		  - The dvergr union, Muspelheim and Niflheim factions build VFE - Medieval 2 settlements, and their tiles are
		    marked unbridgeable.
		This folder only loads when Big and Small - Races is active (see loadFolders.xml); the partner mods are gated
		per operation.
		The mod gates sit on <li> nodes inside sequences, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads
		MayRequire only on list elements.

		Verified against the current 1.6 releases: the frost jotun has neither Alpha Genes gene, the Little People
		faction does list BS_Dwarf at 0.65 in its xenotype chances, the Stoneborn xenotype exists, and all three Norse
		factions already carry a modExtensions list for the settlement options to join.

		A fourth operation was dropped rather than moved: it set Inherit="False" on those three factions' modExtensions.
		Nothing in their parent chain defines modExtensions, so it never did anything. See the removals log.
		Split by category into the MMMM Integrations sub-mods: this copy holds only the Genetics ops (genes and xenotypes).
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="sarg.alphagenes">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BS_FrostJotun"]/genes</xpath>
						<value>
							<li>AG_CryoBlood</li>
						</value>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BS_FrostJotun"]/genes</xpath>
						<value>
							<li>AG_PukeCryo</li>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>

		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
